field.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-01","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Place)","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Communities & Services)","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Corporate Resources)","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Council Acting as Charity Trustees","time":"6.45 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Budget virement of \u00a3341k authorised to fund structural works to council properties following fires, indicating fire damage to HRA stock requiring capital remediation","lead":"Unplanned fire damage to council properties represents material capital liabilities and building safety issues; scope of FRA-related expenditure indicates potential systemic building condition concerns in HRA stock.","iso":"2026-09-11","paper_title":"Appendix 2 for MTFP Update 2026/27 \u2013 2027/28 including Revenue and Capital Forecast at Quarter 1 2026/27","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9891/9891.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Mansfield Connect regeneration project is forecasted to spend only \u00a31m of its \u00a323.7m budget in 2026/27, deferring 96% of planned expenditure to next year","lead":"Massive project slippage indicates execution risk on the council's marquee regeneration scheme and suggests capital delivery challenges that could affect future capital planning and viability of time-sensitive projects.","iso":"2026-09-11","paper_title":"Appendix 2 for MTFP Update 2026/27 \u2013 2027/28 including Revenue and Capital Forecast at Quarter 1 2026/27","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9891/9891.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Development Management facing \u00a3165k overspend driven by use of agency staff to cover vacant posts","lead":"It shows structural staffing challenges that force the council into more expensive labour arrangements. Persistent vacancies in a fee-earning service also risk income loss if processing times increase.","iso":"2026-09-11","paper_title":"MTFP Update 2026/27 \u2013 2027/28 including Revenue and Capital Forecast at Quarter 1 2026/27","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9889/9889.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-11","committee":"Portfolio Holder for Corporate and Finance","paper_title":"Appendix 2 for MTFP Update 2026/27 \u2013 2027/28 including Revenue and Capital Forecast at Quarter 1 2026/27","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9891/9891.pdf","headline":"Budget virement of \u00a3341k authorised to fund structural works to council properties following fires, indicating fire damage to HRA stock requiring capital remediation","detail":"HRA capital programme includes \u00a3341k budget reallocation specifically 'to fund structural works to properties following fires', alongside \u00a31.37m for broader Fire Risk Assessment remedial actions and \u00a32.05m across multiple FRA-related projects for community centres and sheltered housing. The structural works virement suggests actual fire damage requiring capital expenditure beyond routine compliance work.","category":"capital","matters":"Unplanned fire damage to council properties represents material capital liabilities and building safety issues; scope of FRA-related expenditure indicates potential systemic building condition concerns in HRA stock.","figures":"Structural works virement \u00a3341,221; Actions from Fire Risk Assessments budget \u00a31,368,064; Total FRAs and remediation programmes \u00a32,050,816","quote":"Walls 341,221 To fund structural works to properties following fires","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-11","committee":"Portfolio Holder for Corporate and Finance","paper_title":"Appendix 2 for MTFP Update 2026/27 \u2013 2027/28 including Revenue and Capital Forecast at Quarter 1 2026/27","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9891/9891.pdf","headline":"Mansfield Connect regeneration project is forecasted to spend only \u00a31m of its \u00a323.7m budget in 2026/27, deferring 96% of planned expenditure to next year","detail":"The project achieved \u00a3460k actual spend in Q1 against a \u00a323.7m budget. Full-year forecast is \u00a31m, with \u00a322.69m carried forward to 2027/28. This single project accounts for 85% of the council's total General Fund capital carry-forwards, dominating the capital programme timescale.","category":"capital","matters":"Massive project slippage indicates execution risk on the council's marquee regeneration scheme and suggests capital delivery challenges that could affect future capital planning and viability of time-sensitive projects.","figures":"Budget \u00a323,687,138; Forecast 2026/27 \u00a31,000,000; Carry forward to 2027/28 \u00a322,687,138","quote":"Mansfield Connect 23,687,138 459,833 -23,227,305 1,000,000 -22,687,138... Project ongoing to carry on in to the next financial year","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-11","committee":"Portfolio Holder for Corporate and Finance","paper_title":"MTFP Update 2026/27 \u2013 2027/28 including Revenue and Capital Forecast at Quarter 1 2026/27","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9889/9889.pdf","headline":"Development Management facing \u00a3165k overspend driven by use of agency staff to cover vacant posts","detail":"Development Management is forecasting a \u00a3165k overspend due to vacant posts being covered by agency staff, which are significantly more expensive than permanent employees. This reflects wider recruitment difficulties.","category":"people","matters":"It shows structural staffing challenges that force the council into more expensive labour arrangements. Persistent vacancies in a fee-earning service also risk income loss if processing times increase.","figures":"\u00a3165k forecast overspend; agency staff more costly than permanent employees","quote":"The Development Management forecast includes \u00a3165k of additional spend due to agency staff covering vacancies in the service, as agency staff are more costly than permanent employees.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-11","committee":"Portfolio Holder for Corporate and Finance","paper_title":"MTFP Update 2026/27 \u2013 2027/28 including Revenue and Capital Forecast at Quarter 1 2026/27","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9889/9889.pdf","headline":"Section 24 Direction expected by end of 2026 will constrain financial autonomy during LGR transition","detail":"The Local Government Reorganisation process has advanced, with Central Government selecting Option 1Bii. A Structural Changes Order and accompanying Section 24 Direction are expected towards the end of 2026. This direction will require the outgoing council to obtain shadow authority consent for any significant financial commitments.","category":"governance","matters":"This removes financial autonomy at a critical moment when the council is also managing transition costs (estimated \u00a31.1m) and dealing with budget pressures. It will constrain the council's ability to respond to emerging budget challenges.","figures":"Section 24 Direction expected end 2026; LGR transition reserve estimated at \u00a31.1m","quote":"The Secretary of State will also issue a Section 24 Direction, which will prevent outgoing predecessor councils from making significant financial commitments without the consent of the incoming shadow authority.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-11","committee":"Portfolio Holder for Corporate and Finance","paper_title":"MTFP Update 2026/27 \u2013 2027/28 including Revenue and Capital Forecast at Quarter 1 2026/27","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9889/9889.pdf","headline":"Business Rates reset has caused significant permanent reduction in council income requiring reserve depletion","detail":"The Business Rates budgets for 2026/27 and 2027/28 have decreased significantly due to the 2026/27 reset of the business rates system. The council pre-funded a smoothing reserve to manage this impact and is now drawing it down to balance budgets.","category":"income","matters":"Business Rates are a material revenue stream and this permanent structural reduction narrows the council's financial flexibility. Once the smoothing reserve is exhausted, the council will need to find permanent savings or other income to replace it.","figures":"Business Rates budgets decreased significantly; smoothing reserve now being utilised","quote":"The Business Rates budgets for 2026/27 and 2027/28 have decreased significantly compared to recent years due to the reset of the business rates system that took place in 2026/27.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-11"},"name":"Mansfield","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"Budget virement of \u00a3341k authorised to fund structural works to council properties following fires, indicating fire damage to HRA stock requiring capital remediation","lead":"Unplanned fire damage to council properties represents material capital liabilities and building safety issues; scope of FRA-related expenditure indicates potential systemic building condition concerns in HRA stock.","also":["33 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit, Governance & Standards Committee on 2026-09-23","n_findings":34,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 2 for MTFP Update 2026/27 \u2013 2027/28 including Revenue and Capital Forecast at Quarter 1 2026/27","top_paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9891/9891.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":108,"news_drafts_total":3}}